.TH PKERNEL 8 2026-10-25 DarqOS "DarqOS System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
pkernel \- DarqOS pseudo-kernel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkernel
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkernel
is the Linux service that provides the functionality that will
eventually live in the DarqOS kernel.
It keeps the process table, manages IPC ports and each process'
handles for them, keeps the name registry through which processes find
each other's ports, and routes IPC messages between DarqOS processes.
.PP
Every DarqOS process holds a TCP connection to
.B pkernel
on the loopback interface, and uses it to make pseudo-system calls
(p-calls) such as
.BR open_port ,
.BR send_message ,
.B spawn_process
and
.BR kill_process .
.B pkernel
is not itself a DarqOS process: it has no DarqOS process identifier
(dpid).
.PP
On startup,
.B pkernel
listens on TCP port 11000, schedules the boot sequence, and runs its
event loop until interrupted.
.SS Processes
A process is created by a
.B spawn_process
p-call.
.B pkernel
allocates a dpid, then starts
.BR pyloader (8)
from its own directory with that dpid, the parent's dpid, the
listening port, and the executable path.
The executable path must be a directory containing a
.I main.py
file.
The child runs with
.I /
as its working directory, and with the directory containing the
.B darq
package that
.B pkernel
is using prepended to
.BR PYTHONPATH .
.PP
The new process connects back and asks to run with a RUN_REQUEST
message.
.B pkernel
accepts it only for a dpid it has spawned and that has not yet
started: it answers with a RUN_RESPONSE, and only then is the
.B spawn_process
call answered.
For an unknown dpid, or one that is not newly spawned, the
RUN_RESPONSE refuses the request and the connection is closed.
Any other first message also causes the connection to be closed.
.PP
When a process' application finishes, it reports its exit status, and
a description of any failure, in an EXITED message, then closes its
connection.
.B pkernel
records both in the process table, for a future
.B wait
p-call.
.PP
Exited children are reaped on
.BR SIGCHLD .
If a child exits before it sends RUN_REQUEST, its
.B spawn_process
call is answered with an error.
.SS Process states
.TP
.B ALLOCATED
Table entry created, but the process is not yet spawned.
.TP
.B SPAWNED
The loader has been started, but has not sent RUN_REQUEST.
.TP
.B RUNNING
The process is connected and able to make p-calls.
.TP
.B ZOMBIE
The process disconnected after reporting its exit, or after a
.BR kill_process ;
its exit status has not yet been collected.
.TP
.B LOST
The process disconnected without reporting its exit or being killed.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INVOCATION_ID
If set (as it is by
.BR systemd (1)),
log messages are written to standard output without timestamps, for
the journal.
Otherwise they are written to standard error with timestamps.
.TP
.B PYTHONPATH
Passed on to spawned processes, after the
.B darq
package directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /darq/kernel/pkernel
The p-kernel executable.
.TP
.I /darq/kernel/pyloader
Loader for Python executables, started for each new process.
.TP
.I /darq/kernel/darqos-pkernel.service
.BR systemd (1)
unit that runs the p-kernel as part of
.IR darqos.target .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the event loop exits.
.SH BUGS
The listening port is fixed at 11000.
.PP
The boot sequence does not yet start any system services, and
shutdown does not yet stop any processes.
.PP
There is no timeout on a spawned process sending RUN_REQUEST, on a
killed process disconnecting, or on a blocking name lookup.
ZOMBIE entries are never removed from the process table.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pyloader (8),
.BR install (8),
.BR systemd (1)
